I don't think so. I ascend about half as often in SLASH'EM as I did in
NetHack. However, this is mostly due to the early game where you may
encounter too powerful monsters more easily than in NetHack. In fact, I
think SLASH'EM is more balanced than NetHack once you reach the middle
game. In NetHack you may be hunting for one or two missing items
forever, because the RNG simply will not give them to you. And you may
not be able to reach the castle without running the chance of an
instadeath if you do not have one of these items (generating MR or
reflection). In SLASH'EM, you can achieve most ends in more than one
way. There is a guaranteed source of MR in the lawful quest, for
example. It is just difficult to retrieve and awkward to put to action.
But it is not random.

So SLASH'EM makes you less dependent on the RNG, because there are so
many additional branches and item-generating places (which you do not
have to explore, if you got all you need already). Since they are often
difficult to conquer, the game does not get much easier by this, but it
is more -- reliable.

I would call that an increase in balance, not a decrease or absence. If
you are in games that require skill rather than luck, SLASH'EM is
preferable to NetHack.


